# 9. STOCK INTAKE – GOODS RECEIVED NOTE (GRN)

Develop a complete stock intake module.

Stock intake represents goods physically received by a branch.

## GRN functionality

- Generate a unique GRN number automatically.
- Select branch.
- Select supplier.
- Reference purchase order if applicable.
- Record delivery note number.
- Record date received.
- Add multiple products.
- Enter quantities received.
- Automatically fetch product unit cost.
- Allow authorized cost adjustments when necessary.
- Calculate line totals automatically.
- Calculate grand total automatically.
- Record receiving staff.
- Add remarks.
- Save GRN.

## GRN workflow

1. User opens Stock Intake.
2. User creates a new GRN.
3. User selects supplier.
4. User selects branch, subject to permission.
5. User adds products.
6. Product cost is automatically populated.
7. User enters quantities received.
8. The system calculates totals.
9. User reviews and confirms.
10. User saves the GRN.
11. Stock is increased automatically.
12. The transaction is recorded in the stock ledger.
13. Audit log is created.

The stock update must happen only once.

Prevent accidental duplicate submission.

Use database transactions.

