# 25. BUSINESS RULES

Follow these rules carefully:

1. Every product must have a unique product code.
2. Every product must have a stock record for each branch.
3. Products start with zero stock unless opening stock is deliberately recorded.
4. Stock can only increase through valid recorded stock transactions.
5. Stock can only decrease through valid recorded stock transactions.
6. All stock movements must have a transaction reference.
7. Stock intake must increase inventory.
8. Stock issue must decrease inventory.
9. Transfer-out must reduce stock from the source branch.
10. Transfer-in must increase stock at the receiving branch only when the receiving workflow confirms receipt.
11. A stock transfer must never transfer stock to the same branch.
12. Insufficient stock must prevent unauthorized issuance.
13. Stock adjustments must require a reason.
14. GRNs must not be processed twice.
15. Purchase orders do not increase stock.
16. Purchase orders must be reconciled with actual received quantities.
17. Stock alerts must use actual quantities and reorder levels.
18. Branch users must only access permitted branch information.
19. Inventory history must be traceable.
20. Historical transactions must not be casually deleted.
21. All important operations must be audited.
22. All monetary values must be calculated accurately.
23. All critical stock operations must be atomic.
24. Dashboard totals must be calculated from real records.
25. The system must be usable without POS integration.

